  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The agreed watering guidance uses bed observations, and volunteers can leave observations on a board.\", \"decision\": \"How should watering observations lead to assigned work?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers inspect beds and post observations before anyone claims watering work from the board. Assignments follow a shared account of current need.\nVolunteers first claim beds on the board and then inspect those beds before following the watering guidance. Responsibility for observation and any needed work stays together.\nOne volunteer posts bed observations while others claim any resulting watering work from the board. Observation and action can proceed with distinct responsibilities."
    }
  ],
